DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("ln((4*x))");
$fun_1 = Formula("ln((ln((x+5))))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("((2, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (2, infinity))) U (2, infinity)");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-9, -7, -2, 9} U (2, infinity)");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(2, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (2, infinity)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-9, -7, -2, 9})");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("((-infinity, 14)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 14)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 14))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(({-7, 0, 3, 5, 9} U ({-7, 0, 3, 5, 9})) U (-infinity, 14)) U {-7, 0, 3, 5, 9}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`6.58+10-15.48/6.05`] is equal to [_____]{Formula('14.021322314')}
---

[`15.38+17.11`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Real(32.49),width=>5}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-7, 0, 3, 5, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x < 14\}`]

Compute:
- [`(B) \cap B \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`((A \cup (A)) \cup B) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-9, -7, -2, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 1\}`]

Compute:
- [`(B \cap B) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cap B \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -9, -1, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -1, -6, -6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-9, -1, 7>") x Compute("<-1, -6, -6>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-9, -1, 7>") . Compute("<-1, -6, -6>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-1, -6, -6>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-9, -1, 7>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-1, -6, -6>") . Compute("<-9, -1, 7>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 1, 1, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -6, 7, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, 7, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, 7, -8>") x Compute("<1, 1, -9>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, 7, -8>") . Compute("<1, 1, -9>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<1, 1, -9>") . Compute("<-6, 7, -8>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(3) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>3)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>9)}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>7)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
